# ac-av probe: KIND semantics through the formal runner (PLAN-798 V-14,
# K14-01/K14-05 formal legs). A single-function COMPLETE module with a
# direct self-call on the dead branch must keep its module kind across the
# session store: the second `run` step re-requests the SAME source over
# the warm store (cache-hit path) — judged on the LAST run, proving the
# hit path still re-verifies and executes 42 (never a mir.unit-callee
# misclassification, never a cached PASS).

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "av.core.kind-selfcall-module"
  tags: ["ac-av", "probe", "kind"]
  links: ["PLAN-798"]
  source: { text: "fn main() int {
    if false {
        return main()
    } else {
        return 42
    }
}", syntax: "auto", path: "main.at" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "run-kind-fresh-then-hit", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: {
        recipe: "ac-av/core-run-v1",
        av: { entry: "d_main" },
        steps: [ { op: "run" }, { op: "run" } ]
      },
      expect: { completion: "success", exit: 42 } }
  ]
}
```
